  "notes": [
    "Spring blossom set",
    "A squirrel on the branch",
    "New friend: a robin who fluffs and shakes, then lets a blossom fall",
    "New friend: a hedgehog by the basket who sniffs and smiles when a blossom lands",
    "New friend: a caterpillar on the branch who reaches up and nudges a blossom loose",
    "New friend: a bee who loops around her flower while a blossom drifts down",
    "The basket under the branch fills with blossoms as you finish the day's Must do and Should do, and starts fresh each morning",
    "Winter: a snowy branch with red berries, a snowy meadow, and a basket that fills with pinecones (December to February)",
    "New winter friends: a chickadee who puffs up against the cold, and a bunny in a scarf whose ears perk up",
    "More winter friends: a cardinal who hops, a sleepy bear cub who peeks with one eye, and a fox curled in her tail",
    "Christmas: fairy lights on Christmas Eve; colorful lights and a snowman friend on Christmas Day",
    "Autumn (September to November): a branch with orange and gold leaves, a meadow with mushrooms and a little pumpkin, and a basket that fills with acorns. The squirrel is back",
    "New autumn friends: a sleepy owlet who blinks awake, and a chipmunk who puffs her cheeks",
    "New autumn friend: a raccoon by the basket. Special days: a turkey on Thanksgiving; on Halloween a black cat walks along the branch and a pumpkin scarecrow tips his hat",
    "Summer (June to August): a leafy branch with berries, a daisy meadow, and a basket that fills with berries. Holiday friends now stand at the right edge of the page",
    "Summer friends: a bluebird who flutters, a mouse who lets her strawberry go, and a butterfly on a daisy by the basket",
    "New summer friend: a fawn by the basket who looks up and smiles"
  ],
